=== Coverage and limits ===
Thirteen lifecycle tests and all previous fifty-three tests pass in this fresh isolated process.
Lifecycle time tests use actual World Tick at dt=0.1; column/saturation/bounds use dt=0.01, once per automation frame without changing global frame counters.
Passing assertions verify yellow warning after 25 accumulated idle seconds, actual Held survival beyond forty gameplay seconds, pause freeze, drop/throw continuation and thirty-second cumulative expiry.
Capacity-only/clock fixtures disable unrelated free fall. Column support and normal ProjectileMovement/Timer run through real World Tick.
Projectile immediate-release unit case deliberately submits one synthetic blocking Hit; deferred reservation/cancellation is tested before BeginPlay. Existing T12 regression separately verifies real swept impacts.
Full protected budget uses twenty-four actual holders/devices; total admission never removes Held/Active. Separate test covers oldest Dormant retirement, Active order and reentrant retirement/reset.
Column cap test observes real solid support, forced retraction immediately closes support, and reset destroys the already-retracting derived column.
Saturation asserts every frame <=64; blocked planned shots consume attempts, quota release allows the next normal slot, original twelve attempts/duration remain finite.
Explicit safety box removes Held/Active/P01; default WorldSettings fallback is implemented but not independently staged as a separate KillZ test.
Reset covers managed Dormant/Held/Active/Spent/P01 and independent worlds; no full wave/victory/loss/player-ammo restart or final arena configuration is claimed.
Saved Blueprint classes and current GameMode controller were loaded and admit once; existing Blueprints inherit LifecycleFeedback. This is a configuration/native check, not graphical readability proof.
Primary editor session and locked workspace DLL are left untouched. Primary normal link and current graphical Murdock PIE remain pending.
Formal enemy/drops, final arena/cross-wave/full round restart, HUD, independent package, frame-rate/long-run checks and complete G2 remain pending.
No push or PR created for T13; original BP_MothPlayer local change is excluded from commits.
